VK: no queue family ownership transfer on VK_SHARING_MODE_CONCURRENT images.

CommandBufferVK::Barrier writes srcQueue's and dstQueue's family indices into the image barrier
whenever they are given, whatever sharing mode the image was created with. A queue family ownership
transfer is defined only for VK_SHARING_MODE_EXCLUSIVE images, or for VK_SHARING_MODE_CONCURRENT
images with the external (or foreign) family on one side and VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_IGNORED on the other
(NRIDescs.h: "Queue ownership transfer is potentially needed only for SharingMode::EXCLUSIVE
textures"). The Khronos layer tracks any barrier whose two indices differ as a transfer. Measured on
v190, NVIDIA, layer 1.4.341, graphics, compute and copy queues fetched, CONCURRENT images: a release
on the copy queue that transitions COPY_DESTINATION -> COPY_SOURCE and an acquire on the graphics
queue that names COPY_SOURCE -> COPY_SOURCE is VUID-vkCmdDraw-None-09600 at submit ("expects ...
VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_TRANSFER_SRC_OPTIMAL--instead, current layout is VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_TRANSFER_DST_OPTIMAL");
with best practices on, a hand-off of a sampled-only image is
BestPractices-PipelineBarrier-unneeded-QFOT, once for the release and once for the acquire.

TextureVK records the number of active queue families when it is constructed, right before Create,
and so knows the sharing mode DeviceVK::FillCreateInfo chose. For a CONCURRENT image every side that
is not the external family becomes VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_IGNORED: a hand-off between two queues is an
ordinary barrier on each queue, and a release to (or acquire from) the external family keeps the
external side only. EXCLUSIVE images are unchanged. A wrapped VkImage (CreateTextureVK, swap chain
images) has no known sharing mode and keeps the previous behaviour. Buffer barriers already pass
VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_IGNORED.

